1.	Focus on php script (executable simply applies script to given arguments)

2.	Script contains 2 functions 'y' and 'x'.
	'x' uses the exploitable /e modifier from preg_replace --> /e modifier treats the replacement string as PHP code and executes it.

3.	To properly exploit this:	- create a file containing the pattern searched by 'x' which is [x toBeReplaced]
								- [x ${`getflag`}] will give us the flag
								- simply writing `getflag` will not work because y() function encases everything with double quotes ("), using ${} explicitely tells PHP to do substition and look at the content of ${} as code. 

4.	Run the executable with the created file
